    "result_text": "I agree with the finding and fixed both stale cross-references in `Owner.java`:\n\n- **`regionOf` javadoc (line ~206)** \u2014 dropped the \"city fallback of `{@link #getLocality() locality}`\" clause. `getLocality()` no longer calls `regionOf(...)`, so its only remaining role is the create-time postcode range check; the doc now points there (`ValidateOwnerPostcode`) instead of linking to a method that contradicts it.\n\n- **`postcodeRangeOf` javadoc (line ~219)** \u2014 tightened \"`{@link #regionOfPostcode(String) locality derivation}`\" to describe what's now actually true: it's the postcode-to-region lookup that feeds the customerCode's region (and hence the locality, indirectly), not a direct locality derivation.\n\nBoth are comment-only changes with no behavioural impact. Full suite re-run: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures/errors \u2014 acceptance behaviour intact.",
