    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new logic is in the right units and reads coherently: `getLocality()` now reads the region off the customer code the same way `getCheckDigit()` already reads its digits off it, `AuditOwnerCreated` needs no change because it already logs `customerCode`, and the `hash8` helper is a reasonable private detail of `AssignCustomerCode`. One stale cross-reference was left behind, though.\n\nFinding \u2014 dangling javadoc on `Owner.regionOf` (`Owner.java:206-211`):\n\nThe method's javadoc still declares it \"The single source of truth for **both the city fallback of {@link #getLocality() locality}** and the create-time postcode range check.\" This change deleted the city fallback from `getLocality()` entirely \u2014 `getLocality()` no longer calls `regionOf(...)` at all, and the only remaining caller is `ValidateOwnerPostcode` (the postcode range check). The javadoc now advertises a relationship that no longer exists, and it links to `getLocality()` whose own (updated) doc contradicts it. A maintainer reading `regionOf` would be misled about where/whether locality still depends on the city table.\n\nSuggested fix: update `regionOf`'s javadoc to drop the \"city fallback of locality\" clause, so it describes its sole remaining role (the create-time postcode range check in `ValidateOwnerPostcode`). While there, the \"{@link #regionOfPostcode(String) locality derivation}\" phrasing on `postcodeRangeOf` (line 219) is now only indirectly true (region flows through the customer code), so it's worth a quick tightening too.",
